upstream notice and states that it is modified, as Apache-2.0 section 4 requires.

The libjpeg-turbo pin is the commit `e14cbfaa85529d47f9f55b0f104a579c1061f9ad` of
`chromium/deps/libjpeg_turbo` that `third_party/skia/DEPS` names for m156. The C oracle
for `skia-rust-libjpeg` is built from that commit by `oracle/codec-diff/libjpeg/build.sh`.

A row whose crate is not yet in the workspace is a planned port (docs/design/codecs.md
§3); its licence file is added with the crate. The Rust-backed codecs Skia can use
(png, zune-jpeg, jpeg-encoder) are dependencies, not ports, and are listed in Cargo.lock.

